{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",

  "_comment_overview": [
    "Claude Code settings for the Yale YCRC McCleary HPC cluster.",
    "Philosophy: SECURITY FIRST. Prompt for confirmation on anything destructive.",
    "These settings favor safety over speed — you will be asked before writes,",
    "deletions, and most network access.",
    "",
    "DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT: Always prefer conda/mamba for installing packages.",
    "Use pip only when a package is not available via conda-forge. When creating",
    "environments, use: conda create -n <env> -c conda-forge <packages>",
    "For reproducibility, export: conda env export > environment.yml",
    "",
    "LOGIN NODE POLICY: Lightweight orchestration (e.g. snakemake dispatching",
    "jobs to SLURM, git, file inspection, conda env management) is fine on login",
    "nodes. Heavy computation (actual data processing, model training, large I/O)",
    "MUST be submitted as SLURM jobs."
  ],

  "_comment_cluster_info": [
    "=== McCleary Cluster Quick Reference ===",
    "",
    "SSH access:        ssh mccleary.ycrc.yale.edu",
    "Transfer node:     transfer-mccleary.ycrc.yale.edu",
    "Web portal (OOD):  ood-mccleary.ycrc.yale.edu",
    "Docs:              https://docs.ycrc.yale.edu/clusters/mccleary/",
    "Help:              hpc@yale.edu",
    "",
    "=== Storage (DO NOT run heavy I/O on login nodes) ===",
    "",
    "Home:     ~/                     125 GB, 500K files, backed up, snapshotted",
    "Project:  ~/project              /gpfs/gibbs/project — 4 TB shared per group, snapshotted",
    "Scratch:  ~/palmer_scratch       /vast/palmer/scratch — large, PURGED after 60 days",
    "PI alloc: /gpfs/gibbs/pi/<grp>   or /vast/palmer/pi/<grp> (purchased storage)",
    "",
    "Check quotas:         getquota",
    "List your paths:      mydirectories",
    "Disk usage analysis:  module load QDirStat  (use sparingly on large trees)",
    "",
    "=== Slurm Quick Reference ===",
    "",
    "Submit batch job:     sbatch my_job.sh",
    "Interactive job:      salloc -p devel -t 2:00:00 --mem=8G",
    "List your jobs:       squeue --me",
    "Cancel a job:         scancel <jobid>",
    "Job status:           sacct -j <jobid>",
    "Job efficiency:       jobstats <jobid>",
    "Test start estimate:  sbatch --test-only my_job.sh",
    "",
    "=== Common Partitions ===",
    "",
    "devel:      short interactive/test jobs (default for salloc)",
    "day:        up to 24h, general purpose",
    "week:       up to 7 days",
    "long:       up to 30 days",
    "gpu:        GPU jobs (use --gpus flag)",
    "gpu_devel:  short GPU test jobs",
    "bigmem:     high-memory jobs",
    "scavenge:   preemptible, uses idle private nodes",
    "ycga:       YCGA-related work (exempt from compute charges)",
    "",
    "Default walltime is 1 hour on ALL partitions.",
    "Job rate limit: 200 submissions per hour.",
    "Interactive OOD apps: max 4 simultaneous instances.",
    "",
    "=== Batch Script Template ===",
    "",
    "#!/bin/bash",
    "#SBATCH --job-name=my_job",
    "#SBATCH --partition=day",
    "#SBATCH --time=4:00:00",
    "#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=4",
    "#SBATCH --mem-per-cpu=5G",
    "#SBATCH --mail-type=ALL",
    "#SBATCH --output=slurm-%j.out",
    "",
    "module purge",
    "module load <your_software>",
    "<your_command>",
    "",
    "=== GPU Job Example ===",
    "",
    "#!/bin/bash",
    "#SBATCH --partition=gpu",
    "#SBATCH --gpus=1",
    "#SBATCH --time=8:00:00",
    "#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=4",
    "#SBATCH --mem-per-cpu=5G",
    "",
    "module purge",
    "module load CUDA miniconda",
    "conda activate myenv",
    "python train.py",
    "",
    "=== Important Policies ===",
    "",
    "- NEVER run heavy computation on login nodes (login1.mccleary, etc.)",
    "- Lightweight orchestration IS OK on login nodes: snakemake dispatching,",
    "  git operations, conda env management, file inspection, editing scripts",
    "- Request only the resources your job actually needs",
    "- Use 'module load' for software, not manual installs in PATH",
    "- Scratch files older than 60 days are AUTOMATICALLY DELETED",
    "- Do NOT artificially extend scratch file expiration",
    "- Use job arrays or Dead Simple Queue (dsq) for many similar jobs",
    "- McCleary is being decommissioned in 2026 — Bouchet is the successor",
    "",
    "=== Snakemake + SLURM Workflow ===",
    "",
    "Snakemake uses --executor slurm (snakemake-executor-plugin-slurm).",
    "Each rule becomes an independent SLURM job; Snakemake handles dependency",
    "ordering and job submission automatically. The snakemake process itself",
    "runs on the login node as a lightweight orchestrator — this is acceptable.",
    "",
    "Install (once):    conda create -n snakemake -c conda-forge -c bioconda snakemake snakemake-executor-plugin-slurm",
    "Activate:          conda activate snakemake",
    "",
    "Dry run first:     snakemake -n --executor slurm",
    "Run:               snakemake --executor slurm --jobs 50",
    "",
    "Set per-rule resources in your Snakefile:",
    "  rule align:",
    "      resources:",
    "          slurm_partition='day',",
    "          runtime=240,           # minutes",
    "          mem_mb=20000,",
    "          cpus_per_task=4,",
    "          slurm_extra=\"'--mail-type=FAIL'\"",
    "",
    "Or set defaults in a profile (recommended):",
    "  mkdir -p ~/.config/snakemake/slurm",
    "  Create ~/.config/snakemake/slurm/config.yaml:",
    "    executor: slurm",
    "    jobs: 50",
    "    default-resources:",
    "      slurm_partition: day",
    "      runtime: 60",
    "      mem_mb: 5000",
    "      cpus_per_task: 1",
    "    latency-wait: 120",
    "",
    "Then run with profile: snakemake --profile slurm",
    "",
    "For GPU rules, add to resources:",
    "  slurm_partition='gpu', slurm_extra=\"'--gpus=1'\"",
    "",
    "Use tmux when running snakemake on login nodes to survive disconnects:",
    "  tmux new -s pipeline",
    "  conda activate snakemake",
    "  snakemake --executor slurm --jobs 50",
    "  (Ctrl-b d to detach, tmux attach -t pipeline to reconnect)",
    "",
    "=== Conda Environment Management ===",
    "",
    "Prefer conda/mamba over pip wherever possible.",
    "Always use conda-forge as the primary channel.",
    "",
    "Create env:        conda create -n myenv -c conda-forge python=3.11 <pkgs>",
    "From file:         conda env create -f environment.yml",
    "Export env:        conda env export > environment.yml",
    "List envs:         conda env list",
    "Activate:          conda activate myenv",
    "Add package:       conda install -c conda-forge <pkg>",
    "Pip fallback:      pip install <pkg>   (only if not in conda-forge)",
    "Remove env:        conda env remove -n myenv",
    "",
    "Store envs in ~/project or home, NOT in scratch (they'll be purged)."
  ],

  "permissions": {
    "defaultMode": "plan",

    "_comment_defaultMode": [
      "Starts in plan mode: Claude can read and analyze but cannot modify or execute.",
      "Switch to acceptEdits mode with shift+tab when you're ready for Claude to act.",
      "This prevents accidental writes to shared filesystems or unintended job submissions."
    ],

